# Grouper Provider

The Grouper provider manages [Internet2 Grouper](https://www.internet2.edu/products-services/trust-identity/grouper/)
folders (stems), groups, and direct memberships through the Grouper Web Services
REST API.

Use it to keep the groups an application or team depends on in version control:
create the folder structure, define the groups, and add the people (or nested
groups) that belong in them, all reviewed and applied like any other
infrastructure change.

## What it manages

| Type        | Name                                                  | Purpose                                         |
| ----------- | ----------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |
| Resource    | [`grouper_stem`](resources/stem)                      | A folder (stem)                                 |
| Resource    | [`grouper_group`](resources/group)                    | A group                                         |
| Resource    | [`grouper_membership`](resources/membership)          | One direct membership of a subject in a group   |
| Data source | [`grouper_stem`](data-sources/stem)                   | Look up an existing folder                      |
| Data source | [`grouper_group`](data-sources/group)                 | Look up an existing group                       |
| Data source | [`grouper_subject`](data-sources/subject)             | Resolve a person or group to its Grouper subject |

Memberships are managed **one at a time**: each `grouper_membership` adds exactly
one direct member and removes only that member on destroy. Members added by
hand, by the Grouper Loader, or by another tool are never touched. See
[Understanding memberships](guides/memberships) for how this interacts with
effective, nested, and loader-managed membership.

The provider deliberately does **not** manage privileges, attribute definitions,
composite groups, loader jobs, or provisioning.

