## Authentication

The provider authenticates to Grouper Web Services with HTTP Basic
authentication using a Grouper account. Supply credentials through environment
variables so they never appear in configuration or state:

```shell
export GROUPER_BASE_URL="https://grouper.example.edu/grouper-ws/servicesRest"
export GROUPER_USERNAME="terraform-svc"
export GROUPER_PASSWORD="..."
```

Use a dedicated account that holds only the privileges Terraform needs on the
folders it manages. The [authentication guide](guides/authentication) lists
them.

## Environment variables

| Variable                  | Equivalent attribute | Default    |
| ------------------------- | -------------------- | ---------- |
| `GROUPER_BASE_URL`        | `base_url`           | (required) |
| `GROUPER_USERNAME`        | `username`           |            |
| `GROUPER_PASSWORD`        | `password`           |            |
| `GROUPER_REQUEST_TIMEOUT` | `request_timeout`    | `30s`      |

A value set in the provider block takes precedence over the environment.

## Compatibility

| Grouper | Web Services version (`ws_version`) | Status                         |
| ------- | ----------------------------------- | ------------------------------ |
| 4.16    | `v2_6_000` (default)                | Verified by acceptance tests   |

Other Grouper releases that serve the `v2_6_000` API are expected to work but
have not been verified. If your deployment needs a different version segment,
set `ws_version`. Reports of results against other versions are welcome as
[GitHub issues](https://github.com/notlimahrelyt/terraform-provider-grouper/issues).

## Security considerations

- Terraform state contains group names, UUIDs, and subject identifiers. Store
  state in an encrypted, access-controlled backend.
- Credentials are never written to state or logs.
- TLS certificates are verified by default. `insecure_skip_verify` exists only
  for development servers with self-signed certificates.
- Manage each Grouper object from exactly one Terraform state. Two
  configurations managing the same group will fight over it.

